From aa9b98f23419b7a5789d0fd3e1a56df458c4767e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:50:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Serve the DeepSeek V4.1 target head from exact 12-bit packed
 BF16

Upstream base: 04c30fa98e7917fee0a24c739ea503ce1e22538d, after the
spark3 vLLM 0001-0026 series and 0027-explicit-collective-policy.
Requires B12X's packed_bf16_vocab_projection.

The BF16 vocabulary head is read in full for every target verification and
every first draft position, so its cost is its bytes. With
VLLM_DS41_PACKED_BF16_LM_HEAD=1 the DS4.1 target head (which a DSpark
drafter without its own head shares) loads its checkpoint BF16 tensor
unchanged and then packs it with B12X: one sign-and-mantissa byte plus a
4-bit exponent code per value, with out-of-window values kept exactly in a
per-row exception list. The packed bytes replace the BF16 tensor, so the
display carve-out moves them like any streamed weight. The logits
processor declares, prepares and runs B12X's packed projection per token
capacity, as it does the BF16 one.

Quality: lossless. Packing refuses to start unless unpacking reproduces
every bit, and each logit is the exact BF16 products accumulated in FP32
in a fixed order, so a token's logits are the same bits at any batch size.
Logits differ from cuBLAS BF16 only by accumulation order.
Tests: the packed head loads, round-trips exactly, matches BF16 logits,
keeps a token's logits bit-identical across batch sizes, is shared by the
drafter's logits processor and replays in a CUDA graph; the existing
shared and Markov logits-head preparation test still passes.
Upstream status: local experimental patch, not submitted.
